From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: psigod <psigod@example.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 15:11:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] selinux: don't check firmware loads (Android's policy lacks
 firmware_load)

Linux checks direct firmware reads against system:firmware_load. Android's
policy (Android 16 included) has no such permission and is built with
handle_unknown=deny, so under an enforcing policy every firmware load was
refused: GPU microcode and zap shader, Venus, the DSPs, Wi-Fi and
Bluetooth. Skip the check for firmware, as before the permission existed;
modules, kexec, policy and certificate loads are still checked. Linux
userspace without SELinux (postmarketOS) is not affected.
---
 security/selinux/hooks.c | 9 ++++++---
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/security/selinux/hooks.c b/security/selinux/hooks.c
index 30776b0..decdf1a 100644
--- a/security/selinux/hooks.c
+++ b/security/selinux/hooks.c
@@ -4539,8 +4539,12 @@ static int selinux_kernel_read_file(struct file *file,
 			 "New kernel_read_file_id introduced; update SELinux!");
 
 	switch (id) {
+	/*
+	 * Firmware loads are not checked: Android's policy (up to Android 16 at
+	 * least) has no system:firmware_load and denies unknown permissions,
+	 * so every firmware load failed under an enforcing policy.
+	 */
 	case READING_FIRMWARE:
-		rc = selinux_kernel_load_from_file(file, SYSTEM__FIRMWARE_LOAD);
 		break;
 	case READING_MODULE:
 	case READING_MODULE_COMPRESSED:
@@ -4576,8 +4580,7 @@ static int selinux_kernel_load_data(enum kernel_load_data_id id, bool contents)
 			 "New kernel_load_data_id introduced; update SELinux!");
 
 	switch (id) {
-	case LOADING_FIRMWARE:
-		rc = selinux_kernel_load_from_file(NULL, SYSTEM__FIRMWARE_LOAD);
+	case LOADING_FIRMWARE:	/* not checked, see selinux_kernel_read_file() */
 		break;
 	case LOADING_MODULE:
 		rc = selinux_kernel_load_from_file(NULL, SYSTEM__MODULE_LOAD);
